data orch_emit_refusal_reaches_committed_bytes_unobserved: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "orch_emit_refusal_reaches_committed_bytes_unobserved",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.ci_workflow_run_emit", decl_name: "ci_workflow_run_emit_pipeline"),
    requirement: "an orchestration run-body emit that cannot render its pipeline returns a typed, located refusal through the job-body chain unwrapped once at the artifact boundary, rather than rendering a __GUNBC_ORCH_EMIT_REFUSED__ marker that NO artifact-boundary gate scans -- today only one narrow witness asserts the token absent on the compiler-gate contract-stamp script, so a refusal in any other committed workflow's run body is silently committed as a passing step",
    standing: RequirementEstablished { by: orch_emit_refusal_reaches_committed_bytes_unobserved_review },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.ci_workflow_run_emit", decl_name: "ci_workflow_run_emit_pipeline"),
    tail: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.ci_workflow_run_emit", decl_name: "ci_workflow_run_emit_refused_poison"),
    ],
  },
  question: "does any gate at the artifact boundary observe __GUNBC_ORCH_EMIT_REFUSED__? It does not -- only test.claim.compiler_gate_contract_stamp_witness asserts the token absent on one script; gunbc.tier_o_artifact_emit scans only the __GUNBC_INVOKE_EMIT_REFUSED__ family. When ci_workflow_run_emit_pipeline returns a typed Outcome (the same cutover as the invoke emitter), delete the poison and that witness's string_contains together so no orch refusal can be committed unobserved.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "723fc05d265c4a0b9a97a3a73e0d6f58b1b2d28a",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.ci_workflow_run_emit", decl_name: "ci_workflow_run_emit_pipeline") },
        tail: [
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.compiler_gate_contract_stamp_witness", decl_name: "the_generated_step_has_no_warning_arm_and_no_override_input_holds") },
        ],
      },
      account: "Recorded while integrating emitter_string_return_carries_no_typed_refusal. The operator asked, for the orch sentinel, whether anything observes it in rendered output. grep over the tree finds the token __GUNBC_ORCH_EMIT_REFUSED__ asserted absent in exactly one claim (the compiler-gate contract-stamp witness, a per-script assertion) and named in a comment beside fleet_keypair_mint's own token; gunbc.tier_o_artifact_emit.tier_o_workflow_produced scans only the invoke-family prefix. So the orch refusal is unobserved at the artifact boundary outside that one witness. Out of scope for the invoke-emitter PR (its producer is a different module and a different token); recorded so it is not left silent, to be dispatched as its own Outcome cutover.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  disposition: Open,
